* provenance: 2N3904 NPN general-purpose amplifier datasheet 2N3904-D (revised August 2021), onsemi (Fairchild), https://www.onsemi.com/download/data-sheet/pdf/2n3904-d.pdf; 2N5088 NPN general-purpose amplifier datasheet 2N5088-D, onsemi, https://www.onsemi.com/download/data-sheet/pdf/2n5088-d.pdf; values read from the electrical characteristics tables at TA = 25 C
* fit: 2N3904: hFE 200 and VBE 0.655 V at IC = 1 mA, VCE = 5 V; the sheet gives hFE 70 min at IC = 1 mA, 100..300 at IC = 10 mA, and VBE(sat) 0.65..0.85 V at IC = 10 mA. 2N5088: hFE 500 and VBE 0.601 V at IC = 1 mA, VCE = 5 V; the sheet gives hFE 350 min at IC = 1 mA, 300..900 at IC = 0.1 mA, and VBE(on) 0.8 V max at IC = 10 mA. Measured in ssp at 27 C: VBE = 0.655 V gives IC = 1.001 mA and hFE = 200.0 for Q2N3904; VBE = 0.601 V gives IC = 1.001 mA and hFE = 500.0 for Q2N5088
* author: 4esv
* license: MIT

* The sheets tabulate the small-signal region with hFE and VBE(on) only, so each model carries only
* IS (the base-emitter fit) and BF (the hFE fit). No Early voltage, no leakage currents, no
* capacitances: the sheets state none of those at 1 mA, and a number that is not on the sheet is not
* in the model.

* IS is the saturation current that puts VBE at the fit point: VBE = Vt * ln(IC / IS).
.model Q2N3904 NPN (IS=1e-14 BF=200)
.model Q2N5088 NPN (IS=8e-14 BF=500)
